TI Dual main-group metal doping in covalent organic polymers boosts hydrogen evolution via interlayer coupling engineering: A machine learning aided density functional theory (DFT) investigation
SO INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF HYDROGEN ENERGY
LA English
DT Article
DE Interlayer coupling electrocatalysis; Main-group metal; HER; M-1/COPs@M-2/COPs; Machine learning
ID FEATURE-SELECTION; PREDICTION; CATALYSTS; REGRESSION; SETS
AB Developing efficient non-precious metal catalysts for the hydrogen evolution reaction (HER) remains a critical challenge. In this study, we design a novel class of heterostructured catalysts by synergistically integrating main-group metal doping with interlayer coupling in two-dimensional covalent organic polymers (COPs). Density functional theory calculations reveal that the M1/COPs@M2/COPs heterostructures possess metallic conductivity and exhibit near-optimal hydrogen adsorption free energy (Delta GH* approximate to 0 eV), with 8 candidates such as Ge/ COPs@Sb/COPs demonstrating exceptional HER activity. The enhanced catalytic performance originates from interlayer charge redistribution and p-orbital-mediated hydrogen adsorption. Furthermore, machine learning analysis identifies charge transfer as the key descriptor governing catalytic activity. This work provides atomic-level insights into the cooperative effects of doping and interlayer coupling, establishing a generalizable strategy for the rational design of high-performance electrocatalysts.
