TI Hybrid substitution workflows should accelerate the uptake of chemical recyclates in polymer formulations
SO CURRENT OPINION IN GREEN AND SUSTAINABLE CHEMISTRY
LA English
DT Article
DE Polymer formulation; Machine learning; Molecular dynamics; Experimental design
ID MOLECULAR-DYNAMICS; PLASTICS; OPPORTUNITIES; MODELS
AB Chemical recycling of polymers is taking off as a circular technology, typically targeting pure recyclates. However, this is often not achieved efficiently due to high energy demand of separation and purification steps. In addition, many polymer applications have complex formulations that may be sensitive to impure feedstocks. Substitution of virgin feedstocks by complex recyclates (often containing impurities) requires a good knowledge of the structure/composition-property re-lations of polymer formulations. As this is often not the case, current practice relies on costly and rather inefficient enumeration experiments, or, at best, classical design-of-experiments approaches. We review the state-of-the art in structure-property modeling, present an example for poly-urethane formulations, and propose a hybrid model-based framework. This involves a machine learning workflow for substitution problems in complex polymer formulations, combining existing data, novel reaction kinetics, structure-property models, molecular dynamics, and a mini-mum of experimental-analytical data where necessary, to build and validate the model.
C1 [Kovacs, Attila; Nimmegeers, Philippe; Billen, Pieter] Univ Antwerp, Fac Appl Engn Intelligence Proc Adv Catalysts & So, B-2020 Antwerp, Belgium.; [Nimmegeers, Philippe] Univ Antwerp, Fac Business & Econ, Dept Engn Management, Environm Econ EnvEcon, B-2000 Antwerp, Belgium.; [Nimmegeers, Philippe] VCCM Core Lab, B-2000 Antwerp, Belgium.; [Cunha, Ana] Univ Antwerp, Fac Sci, Dept Chem, MOLSPEC, B-2020 Antwerp, Belgium.; [Brancart, Joost] Vrije Univ Brussel, Phys Chem & Polymer Sci FYSC, B-1050 Brussels, Belgium.; [Mansouri, Seyed Soheil] Tech Univ Denmark, Dept Chem & Biochem Engn, Soltofts Plads,Bldg 228A, DK-2800 Lyngby, Denmark.; [Gani, Rafiqul] PSE SPEED Co, Ordrup Jagtvej 42D, DK-2920 Charlottenlund, Denmark.; [Gani, Rafiqul] Hong Kong Univ Sci & Technol Guangzhou, Sustainable Energy & Environm Thrust, Guangzhou, Peoples R China.
