TI Therapeutic effect of Cu(II) coordination polymer on acute asthma and ligand optimization using machine learning algorithms
SO JOURNAL OF MOLECULAR STRUCTURE
LA English
DT Article
DE Coordination polymer; Acute asthma; NF-?B; RT-PCR; Deep learning
ID ORGANIC FRAMEWORK; EFFICIENT; DOCKING
AB Via using the mixed-ligand synthesis approach, a novel Cu(II)-bearing coordination polymer with the chemical composition of {[Cu-3(phen)(2)(HL)(2)]middot(H2O)(2)}(n) (1) (H4L = 3,3 ',5,5 '-azoxybenzenetetracarboxylic acid, phen = Phenanthroline) was successfully prepared by reaction of Cu(NO3)(2)middot3H(2)O with the carboxylic acid and N-chelating ligands under solvothermal conditions. Its therapeutic effect and mechanism on acute asthma was explored and the related mechanism was explored at the same time. Firstly, the IFN-gamma and IL-5 released by the bronchial endothelial cells was measured with ELISA assay. In addition to this, the activation levels of the NF-kappa B signaling pathway were also determined with real time RT-PCR assay. The optimized ligands through the deep learning method exhibit excellent biological effects, which shed light on the novel, artificial intelligence supported strategy for drug discovery. (C) 2022 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.
