PT J
AU Gao, SZ
   Yan, JL
   Bai, ZK
AF Gao, Shuzhi
   Yan, Jinlin
   Bai, Zikang
TI A soft sensor for VCM conversion rate in PVC polymerization using a HEFLA-optimized BERT-xLSTM-Mamba deep learning network
SO CHEMICAL ENGINEERING SCIENCE
LA English
DT Article
DE Soft-sensor; PVC polymerization process; Deep learning; Extended long short-term memory network; Mamba network; Fick's law algorithm
ID NEURAL-NETWORK; MODEL
AB To address the undirectly measurable vinyl chloride monomer (VCM) conversion rate in polyvinyl chloride (PVC) polymerization, this paper proposes a functional decoupling hybrid deep learning soft sensor model, HEFLA-BERT-xLSTM-Mamba. It tackles three core challenges: global non-stationary trends, local operational transients, and multi-scale noise. Process variables are selected using a CatBoost-based comprehensive feature importance method. A Hybrid Enhancing Fick's Law Algorithm (HEFLA) is introduced to optimise model training. The BERT module captures global long-range dependencies via bidirectional self-attention, xLSTM rapidly responds to local dynamics with exponential gating, and Mamba performs adaptive noise filtering through selective state-space modelling. A gated attention network dynamically integrates the three modules, adjusting weights in real time according to input features. Simulation results demonstrate strong robustness, improved prediction accuracy, and effective real-time control of PVC production. Compared with existing hybrid models, it achieves a superior balance among prediction accuracy, error distribution stability, and computational efficiency, offering an effective soft-sensing solution for complex chemical processes.
