TI Improvement of thermal protection performance of polymer composites based on optimized piecewise porosity distribution using a neural network method
SO THERMAL SCIENCE AND ENGINEERING PROGRESS
LA English
DT Article
DE Optimization; Polymer composite; Thermal protection system; Piecewise porosity distribution; BP neural network
ID MODEL
AB Reentry vehicles, such as returnable satellites and reentry capsules, are subjected to severe aerodynamic heating. Thermal protection system to protect vehicles and crew from ultra-high temperature is critical. Polymer com-posite is one of the most effective thermal protection materials. With the view of improving the thermal pro-tection performance of polymer composites under harsh aerodynamic thermal environment, a model of thermal response of polymer composites without surface recession is established and verified for simulating the ablation process. Based on simulated data, we explore the relationship between piecewise porosity distribution and bondline temperature using machine learning methods. Further, optimal porosity distributions under different number of segments are obtained by taking bondline temperature as the objective function. We find that opti-mized porosity distributions are almost identical under different number of segments. On the premise that the total pore content is the same, three ablators with different porosity distribution are compared with the opti-mized one. Numerical results show that the optimized porosity distribution can reduce the bondline temperature by 17.61 K, indicating that rational optimization of porosity can improve the material utilization rate.
